  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nFirst, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3})+1 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3}) & =-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3}) & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3}) & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi , & \\, & \\, & 2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3} & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{12}+2n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & 2x & =\\frac{43\\pi }{12}+2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{24}+n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{43\\pi }{24}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{24}+\\frac{24n\\pi }{24} & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{43\\pi }{24}+\\frac{24n\\pi }{24} \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi (25+24n)}{24} & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{\\pi (43+24n)}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{25\\pi }{24}$ and $x=\\frac{43\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24}$ and $x=\\frac{19\\pi }{24}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{24},\\frac{19\\pi }{24},\\frac{25\\pi }{24},\\frac{43\\pi }{24}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{24}$ and ${x}_{3}=\\frac{25\\pi }{24},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{24}+\\frac{25\\pi }{24}=\\frac{26\\pi }{24}=\\frac{13\\pi }{12}.\n$$",
